ansport publishes error-bearing futures too by source reading; this check does not execute that transport or byte decoding.\",\n        \"The existing zero-valued timeout response has Success=false and may prevent match advancement despite invalid interface access. The check must not promote the access result to a commit-safety finding.\"\n      ],\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"term\": 4,\n        \"request_index\": 2,\n        \"transport_timeout_ms\": 100,\n        \"scenarios\": [\n          \"timeout\",\n          \"success\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"rationale\": \"Select the previously unresolved pipeline validity relation as a distinct local question. The prior cross-leader ownership explanation is retained. The interface supplies the expectation and actual inmem timeout production supplies a controllable input; no broader protocol violation is assumed.\",\n    \"status\": \"partial\",\n    \"previous_id\": null,\n    \"version\": 1,\n    \"boundary_changes\": [],\n    \"obligation_checks\": {\n      \"failed-pipeline-response-not-consumed\": [\n        \"183d31024372490eaa400890d8fa2127\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\n      \"failed-pipeline-response-not-consumed\"\n    ],\n    \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n    \"semantic_readiness\": {},\n    \"audit_question\": {\n      \"disposition\": \"ready_for_check\",\n      \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n      \"requests\": [],\n      \"question\": \"When built-in InmemTransport publishes a completed AppendFuture with a non-nil timeout error, does Raft.pipelineDecode call Response on that same failed future? The discriminator is a delegated Response access count correlated with the actual Future.Error status after consumer completion.\",\n      \"importance\": \"pipelineDecode uses response fields to accept replication support or reject the pipeline. Reading a response outside its interface validity condition can make support interpretation depend on unspecified error-state fields. The selected endpoint is only failed-future Response access; unsafe support and system consequences remain unestablished.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"pipeline-interface\",\n        \"pipeline-result\",\n        \"replication-update\",\n        \"inmem-pipeline-factory\",\n        \"inmem-pipeline-producer\",\n        \"inmem-pipeline-submit\",\n        \"net-pipeline-producer\",\n        \"net-response-decoder\",\n        \"future-status-contract\",\n        \"future-completion\",\n        \"append-future-access\",\n        \"ordinary-result-control\"\n      ],\n      \"participants\": [\n        \"Raft pipelineDecode consumer\",\n        \"Built-in InmemTransport pipeline producer\",\n        \"A connected in-memory peer with a withheld response\",\n        \"A scripted successful/rejecting peer control\"\n      ],\n      \"objects\": [\n        \"One identified AppendFuture per timeout/success operation\",\n        \"Its independent request identity and response allocation\",\n        \"A delegating future wrapper\",\n        \"Per-scenario followerReplication and commitment\"\n      ],\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"A1 support consumption at AppendFuture interface\",\n        \"One term 4 and fixed two-voter configuration in an isolated consumer fixture\",\n        \"Response delay beyond transport deadline; no Byzantine data or storage failure injection\",\n        \"No leadership replacement: the preceding cross-incarnation question remains explained\"\n      ],\n      \"event_paths\": [\n        \"AppendEntries admits a request into the connected peer transport and registers its actual future with inprogressCh.\",\n        \"The timeout scenario withholds the RPC reply; inmemPipeline.decodeResponses calls respond(error) and publishes the future on doneCh. The success control replies through RPC.Respond and the same producer publishes its future.\",\n        \"The harness retains future identity from submission to Consumer publication without calling Error or Response on the measured future.\",\n        \"A wrapper counts Response calls while delegating all method behavior. pipelineDecode consumes the real completed future through an adapted ready channel.\",\n        \"An independently completed rejection future is queued after the measured future to stop a successful decoding path. Consumer completion is required; timeout is a test infrastructure failure, not a property verdict.\",\n        \"After finishCh closes, the harness reads the actual measured future Error, verifies the intended producer outcome, and emits the Response count for that operation.\"\n      ],\n      \"activity_classes\": [\n        \"A1\"\n      ],\n      \"behavior_ids\": [],\n      \"fact_ids\": [],\n      \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"The ready channel synchronizes completion and may eliminate waiting, but does not make an errored response valid.\",\n        \"A zero-valued timeout response and !resp.Success can prevent log progress even if the Response access precondition is violated.\",\n        \"Ordinary replicateTo checks the transport call error before reading response fields.\",\n        \"Old/new commitment object isolation from the accepted prior question remains intact and does not establish this interface precondition.\"\n      ],\n      \"unknowns\": [\n        \"This check ends at AppendFuture.Response interface access. It does not establish invalid log matching, a false quorum, loss of leader authority, or an unsafe application.\",\n        \"The local consumer is invoked directly with minimal Raft/followerReplication state; election, log persistence and the full replication sender loop are not executed.\",\n        \"The successful control peer is scripted at the RPC interface. Its acknowledgement is not evidence of durable follower storage.\",\n        \"Ready futures are collected from the real InmemTransport pipeline and delivered through a deleg